From 7d7c71a4935d5acb69130665b028b68464805973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:03:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08044/11362] The induce path finally sends a repetition
 penalty -- and the rebuild meant to discharge it would have deleted the
 record

Phase 2 of the induce-reliability investigation: ship what Phase 1 measured.

WHAT SHIPPED (LocalGGUFProposer, scoped to the code-only induce path, both
env-reversible):

  * repeat_penalty 1.1 + repeat_last_n 256 on the /completion payload.
    CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_REPEAT_PENALTY=1.0 restores the old payload byte-for-byte.
  * A defect gate + ONE plain re-ask, via arc_engine_static_validation.
    CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_DEFECT_REASKS=0 disables it, so the two run independently --
    the penalty carries 11 of the 13 paired wins and the re-ask 2.

The re-ask names NOTHING about the defect. repair_prompt_block() exists and was
measured against this neutral block at p = 1.000: the defect TEXT bought nothing,
the second ASK is the whole effect. It stays unwired.

CLAIMED: validity and cost. Usable engines 13/36 -> 22/36 (paired sign test
p = 0.049), 47.2s vs 100.3s per attempt, token-cap hits 20/36 -> 2/36.
NOT CLAIMED: that this fixes induction. Strict out-of-sample quality moved 2/6
games -> 3/6 on one attempt, p = 1.000, on 5 discordant pairs whose best
reachable p was 0.0625. On tu93 and sc25 no arm ever produced a correct engine.

SAFETY INVARIANT: the gate can never turn an accept into a hard failure -- it
spends at most one extra attempt, and only while one remains. My first draft got
this wrong (the continue fell through to the failure return); the mutation check
caught it, not review. It is one of 3 mutations killed by the 13 new tests.

THE REBUILD WAS DESTRUCTIVE, AND THE ARTIFACTS HAD ALREADY SAID SO.
Editing the module marks 7 artifacts stale; 4 carry rebuild commands. I ran all
4. Every one dropped its accumulated freshness_acknowledgements (4/4/4/2 -> 0)
and its original_timings_superseded_by_rebuild block -- which is itself the
record of the LAST time this happened, and which instructs: "When the only drift
is timing, acknowledge rather than rebuild." The rebuilds were discarded, the
published artifacts restored, and all 7 discharged by acknowledgement. Every
results/ diff is +9 -0: not one existing line touched.

The rebuilds became the EVIDENCE instead -- differential execution at the
artifact level, stronger than arguing from the diff. Deep-diffed leaf by leaf:
6011 0/48,488 substantive, 6012 1 (a hash OVER the dependency set), 6013
0/7,390, 6021 4 (aggregation_wall_s + 3 code_provenance). NO published
measurement moved; 6021's head-to-head statistics are identical.

ALSO FOUND: test_artifact_freshness_acknowledgement_2026_07_30.py was silently
RED. It asserted evidence must "name where a reader can check it" as
`"6011" in evidence or "changelog" in evidence` -- and 4 of the 6
acknowledgements on each capture artifact already failed it at HEAD. Now asserts
the property rather than two spellings of it; still rejects a confident
paragraph with nothing behind it (mutation-checked), and it caught my own first
draft. The 2 genuinely location-free 2026-07-30 entries are grandfathered BY
DATE, not rewritten, with their count pinned at exactly 2.

arc_engine_static_validation is now live-path reachable, so its orphan-lint
allow-list entry is retired (verified by unwiring the import and confirming the
lint flags it). The two tests pinning its orphan status inverted, as their own
docstrings had planned for.

The budget single-source patch stays unlanded: measured, it widens the blast
radius 7 -> 12 and drags in a live capture that would overwrite published
numbers.

